cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Structure Without Reading: a reproducible structural analysis of the rongorongo corpus"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rochala
    given-names: Piotr
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-06
repository-code: "https://github.com/rochal/rongorongo"
url: "https://github.com/rochal/rongorongo"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - rongorongo
  - Easter Island
  - Rapa Nui
  - undeciphered scripts
  - corpus analysis
  - digital humanities
abstract: >-
  Scripts, generated tables and a working report analysing the rongorongo
  corpus of Easter Island for structure without assigning meaning to any
  sign. Uses the CEIPP numerical transliteration of Barthel's corpus, Barthel's
  sign catalogue, Thomson's 1891 recitations and Jaussen's 1893 record of
  Metoro's chanted readings. Covers parallel passages and text families,
  delimited lists, alternating series, an affix test for the stroke signs,
  allograph mining, sign inventories, shape similarity, genre clustering,
  sequence entropy, collocations, compound decomposition, comparison with
  Rapa Nui word statistics and the 1886 creation chant, the structure of the
  Santiago Staff, and the consistency of Metoro's readings, each result with
  a control or a shuffled null.
